<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF DOWNHILL WINNER ALPHAND.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF DOWNHILL WINNER ALPHAND.</headline>
<dateline>VAL GARDENA, Italy 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profile of the winner of Friday's men's World Cup downhill:</p>
<p>Name: Luc Alphand</p>
<p>Age: 31</p>
<p>Nation: France</p>
<p>Previous World Cup victories: Six (all downhills) - Kitzbuehel (twice) 1995, Bormio 1995, Vail 1995, Val d'Isere 1995, Garmisch 1996.</p>
<p>Other facts: Won a bronze medal at 1996 world championships in Sierra Nevada. Nicknamed &quot;Lucho&quot;, the easy-going Alphand comes from resort of Serre-Chevalier. Has now won more World Cup downhills than any other Frenchman.</p>
</text>
